q('MPRE Review','Confidentiality',1,'In general, does the attorney-client privilege protect every piece of information related to representation?',['No; ethical confidentiality is broader than the evidentiary privilege','Yes, the concepts are identical','Yes, regardless of context and exceptions','Only if a court sends a written invitation'],0,['Correct: ethical confidentiality and attorney-client privilege cover different scopes.','The two are distinct doctrines.','Privilege has elements and exceptions.','A court invitation is not required.'],'ABA Model Rule 1.6; privilege principles');
